    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Permafrost carbon feedback",
    "problem": "Existing climate models struggle to accurately project carbon release from thawing permafrost because they fail to incorporate complex abrupt thaw processes and are hampered by a lack of observational data from remote environments.",
    "method": "A survey of 41 international scientists was conducted to quantify expert opinion on the magnitude of future permafrost thaw and associated carbon release under several distinct climate warming scenarios and time periods.",
    "task": "The task is to estimate the magnitude and timing of carbon release from thawing permafrost under future warming scenarios by synthesizing the collective knowledge of international experts through a formal survey.",
